[{:adr/consequences "{:shared_bugfixes \"one tested judgment engine, one place bugs get fixed, both FLOW and HARMONY benefit immediately -- mirrors the value already realized this session when porting FLOW to network-isekai surfaced and fixed a real bug in the shared kami-engine-clj compiler\", :flow_repo_shrinks \"ghosthacker-flow's own repo becomes just its host adapters, not a judgment engine that happens to also serve another game\", :portfolio_precedent \"establishes the pattern for any future portfolio title needing the same sync-to-a-beat mechanic (at least #8 DUET is rhythm-adjacent) to depend on this core rather than re-deriving it\", :coordination_cost \"two more repos to keep pins current on versus one -- accepted per :risk above\", :history_not_preserved \"core.cljc's git history in ghosthacker-flow does not follow it to the new repo (fresh file, fresh repo, not a git subtree split) -- judged acceptable for a young, small file\", :harmony_not_built_here \"this ADR resolves only the extraction the Addendum deferred; HARMONY's own design/implementation is separate, immediately-following work\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["ghosthacker-flow.core / ghosthacker.groove.core (the beat-phase/window judging, score/combo/groove-crossfade state transitions, anti-mash guard, miss-on-silence detection, chart-based multi-section support) lives in com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker-groove-core, not duplicated into each game that needs a sync-to-a-beat mechanic" "com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker-flow keeps only its own host adapters (demo.clj, terminal.clj) and depends on ghosthacker-groove-core via a pinned :git/url/:sha deps.edn dependency, not a local copy" "com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker-harmony (Ghost Hacker portfolio #2, ADR-2607023200 row 2, the flagship rhythm game / Ghost Battle proper) depends on the same shared core the same way; HARMONY-specific work is the win/lose Ghost Battle framing (ASYMMETRY/HARMONY derived from grade/accuracy/groove), not a second judgment engine" "this resolves ADR-2607023200's Addendum (2026-07-03), which fixed the direction (share, don't duplicate) but deferred the mechanism to \"HARMONY着手PR\" — this ADR is that PR, choosing option (a) extract-now over option (b) duplicate-then-unify"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "ghosthacker-groove-core-extraction", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607023200-ghosthacker-game-portfolio-flow.md" "com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker-flow" "com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker-groove-core" "com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker-harmony" "manifest/repos.edn"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607032600-ghosthacker-groove-core-extraction", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-03", :adr/decision "{:new_repos [{:path \"com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker-groove-core\", :visibility :private, :contents \"src/ghosthacker_flow/core.cljc + test/ghosthacker_flow/core_test.cljc from ghosthacker-flow, renamed to ghosthacker.groove.core / ghosthacker.groove.core-test (namespace-only rename, zero behavior change)\"} {:path \"com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker-harmony\", :visibility :private, :contents \"new repo, portfolio #2 (this ADR's companion, immediately-following work — not implemented by this ADR itself)\"}], :source_repo_change {:repo \"com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker-flow\", :action \"remove src/ghosthacker_flow/core.cljc + test/ghosthacker_flow/core_test.cljc, add a pinned :git/url/:sha dependency on ghosthacker-groove-core, update demo.clj/terminal.clj's requires from ghosthacker-flow.core to ghosthacker.groove.core\", :unaffected \"demo.clj, terminal.clj, terminal_test.clj, demo_test.clj (FLOW's own host adapters, unchanged besides the require), the network-isekai games/gftd/ghosthacker-flow guest logic.cljc (a from-scratch reimplementation in a different restricted language already, not affected)\"}, :dependency_shape \"deps.edn :git/url + :sha, mirroring the kami-mangaka-* sibling-repo pattern already used across this org for independently-releasable standalone repos (not a monorepo :local/root, since these are genuinely separate repos)\"}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"ADR-2607023200's Addendum found ghosthacker-flow.core had grown into a general four-on-the-floor sync judgment engine with almost nothing FLOW-action-specific in it (38 tests / 133 assertions as of this ADR: judge-with-windows, difficulty-presets, apply-judgment's score/combo/groove state machine, judge-input-once's anti-mash guard, judge-run's miss-on-silence detection, chart-beats/judge-chart-input's multi-section support), and deferred the extract-vs-duplicate decision to whenever HARMONY (portfolio #2, the flagship rhythm game) actually started\", :investigated [\"HARMONY's design brief in ADR-2607023200's table (\\\"四つ打ちに同期し続ける精度を競い、乗れているほどTENSE→Sky Highへ曲が転調していく\\\") is the SAME judgment/crossfade model FLOW already implements, not a variant — confirmed by re-reading both design texts side by side, not assumed\" \"no code anywhere references ghosthacker-flow.core outside ghosthacker-flow itself yet (HARMONY doesn't exist), so extraction now has zero call-site migration risk beyond ghosthacker-flow's own demo.clj/terminal.clj\" \"the org's existing kami-mangaka-* sibling-repo dependency pattern (deps.edn :git/url + :sha across independently-releasable standalone repos) is a direct, already-proven precedent for how ghosthacker-flow and ghosthacker-harmony should both depend on ghosthacker-groove-core\"], :risk \"two more repos to keep in sync (groove-core + harmony) versus one — an ongoing coordination cost (dependency pin bumps when groove-core changes) that duplication would have avoided short-term; judged worth it to prevent a second consumer's timing/scoring math ever forking from the tested original\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"duplicate core.cljc into ghosthacker-harmony now, unify once both implementations exist (option (b) from the Addendum)\", :rejected_because \"with a mature, tested core already sitting in one repo and a second concrete consumer about to exist, extracting first avoids ever letting two copies of hand-tuned timing/scoring math exist as a fork rather than a dependent, even briefly\"} {:option \"keep ghosthacker-flow.core in ghosthacker-flow and have ghosthacker-harmony :git/url-depend directly on ghosthacker-flow\", :rejected_because \"couples HARMONY's judgment engine to FLOW's own repo lifecycle/versioning/README, when the shared logic is host/game-agnostic and belongs to neither game specifically\"} {:option \"history-preserving git subtree split instead of a plain copy + rename\", :rejected_because \"no concrete need for preserved blame history on this small (133-assertion), young file; mirrors this org's existing precedent (ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico's split, ADR-2607011816) of plain-copy + provenance note over history-preserving tooling\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607032600: ghosthacker-groove-core — extract FLOW's judgment engine into a shared repo ahead of HARMONY"}]